Package: swissvotescore
Type: Package
Title: Transform BFS Vote-Result JSON Into Tidy Data Frames
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Thomas", "Lo Russo", email = "th.lorusso@gmail.com", role = "aut"),
    person("Thomas", "Willi", email = "thomas.willi@uzh.ch", role = "aut"),
    person("Leo", "Jöhr", email = "leo.joehr@gmail.com", role = c("cre", "ctb")))
Description: The json-to-data-frame transforms from the swissdd package, factored out
    from their http fetching so that results can be reproduced from an archived copy of
    the data rather than re-fetched. Reads the federal and cantonal vote-result json
    published by the Swiss Federal Statistical Office and returns one tidy data frame at
    the geographical level of choice. Derived from swissdd
    <https://github.com/politanch/swissdd>, GPL (>= 2).
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
Imports:
    dplyr,
    tidyr (>= 1.0.0),
    jsonlite,
    lubridate,
    purrr,
    tibble
URL: https://github.com/oeL2002/swissvotescore
BugReports: https://github.com/oeL2002/swissvotescore/issues
License: GPL (>= 2)
Encoding: UTF-8
NeedsCompilation: no
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
